nts.\n- \"A shared Kanban board with ordered columns, each containing an ordered list of cards.\" - Done.\n- \"Create cards, move cards across columns, and reorder cards within a column via drag-and-drop.\" - Done.\n- \"Persist board state durably on local disk using PGLite.\" - Done (`./pgdata`).\n- \"Broadcast every mutation to all connected clients so boards stay convergent in real time.\" - Done via SSE.\n- \"Optimistic UI: the dragging client updates immediately, then reconciles against the server's authoritative ordering.\" - Done via `dragover` and SSE.\n\nI should make sure `vite` is installed correctly in the client.\n\nLet's test it. Since I can't actually run a browser, I'll just ensure the files are correct.\n\nWait, I noticed one thing. In `client/main.js`, I have:\n```javascript\nconst API_BASE = 'http://localhost:3000/api';\n```\nAnd the server runs on `3000`. This is correct.\n\nThe server uses `cors()` which is necessary because Vite usually runs on port 5173.\n\nLet me check if I need to add any other files.\nMaybe a `.gitignore`? The prompt doesn't ask for it, but it's good practice. I'll skip it unless necessary.\n\nOne detail: \"The backend creates any directory it needs (such as PGLite's data directory)\".\nIn `server/index.js`:\n```javascript\nconst db = new PGLite('./pgdata');\n```\nPGLite handles directory creation.\n\nWait, in `server/index.js`, I used `Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)`. `substr` is deprecated. I should use `substring`.\n\n```javascript\nconst id = Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 11);\n```\n\nLet me fix that.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{\"new_str\":\"    const id = Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 11);\",\"old_str\":\"    const id = Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\",\"path\":\"server/index.js\"}"}}]}
